==Description==
The [[Image:CfdOF_SolverControl.svg|16px]] '''CfdOF SolverControl''' command opens a task panel to solve the analysis using OpenFOAM and open the results in Paraview.
<!--T:3-->

==Usage== <!--T:4-->

=== Solve and View Results ===

# Click {{Button|'''Write Case'''}}
# Click {{Button|'''Run'''}}
#* A plot will open in a new tab to plot residuals. In a steady-state analysis, the solver will continue until all residuals are below a specified value (0.001 by default), or for a specified number of iterations (2000 by default). In a transient analysis, it continues until a specified end time is reached (1.0 s). These defaults can be changed in the Data Tab of the [[Property View]]. The plotted residuals should decrease over time. If they increase (diverge), the results will be inaccurate, but that can sometimes be fixed by improving the mesh quality or changing boundary conditions.
# Click {{Button|'''ParaView'''}}
#* This opens Paraview in a new window for viewing results. ParaView supports color maps, vector fields, and charts. See [https://docs.paraview.org/en/latest/index.html ParaView Documentation] for help.<br />

==Options== <!--T:5-->

When {{CheckBox|TRUE|'''Solve in Parallel'''}} is checked, OpenFOAM will run with multiple CPU cores.

==Notes== <!--T:6-->

OpenFOAM and ParaView must be installed in the locations specified in the CfdOF Preferences Panel. See [[CfdOF Install#Dependency installation|CfdOF Install]].



